      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start and definitely hits the professional notes. \n\ni just ran it through our internal CHM tool real quick to see where we stand before i send it to my boss, and the positivity score is actually sitting a bit lower than i'd like. it's not \"rude\" or anything, but it's kind of a flat, heavy tone. \n\ncan you try a second version? i still need the apology to be real and not ignore the outage, but try to lift the tone a bit more so the sentiment score looks better. just don't go overboard and make it sound fake, i just want it to feel a bit more \"constructive\" and optimistic about our partnership.",
      "source": "evaluator"
